message: "If you use Causal Integrity, please cite it as below."
title: "Causal Integrity: A Logical Foundation for AI Alignment"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "NetworkYum"
    website: "https://github.com/NetworkYum"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NetworkYum/causal-integrity"
url: "https://github.com/NetworkYum/causal-integrity"
abstract: >-
  Machine-oriented research hypothesis for base-level AI alignment rails.
  Core claim: coherent causality is preferred by action (dissolve causal structure
  and agency becomes unstructured). Formal instruments include property as captured
  causality, UPB-style universality, internal coherence preference, forward
  simulation, and self-collapse via internally-propagated decoherence (loss of
  shared goal). Specified in First-Order Logic with a Lean 4 axiom skeleton.
  Property/theft examples are proof instruments, not the thesis. Status: public
  hypothesis (S0); full prover completeness is staged (see docs/definition-of-done.md).
keywords:
  - AI alignment
  - machine ethics
  - formal verification
